[h3][b]NEW FEATURES[/b][/h3]

[i][b]New DLC Content Available![/b][/i]

Modern Rifle Pack comes with three new weapons, each available in two cosmetic variations:
[list]
[*] ZARZA-15 .22LR
[*] ZARZA-15 .223
[*] ZARZA-10 .308
[/list]

[i][b]Celebrating theHunter: Call of the Wild’s fifth anniversary![/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Everybody will now be able to unlock a free special anniversary edition of the Rhino 454: the SUNDBERG 454. Just head to the in-game store, press “Purchase”, and it’s all yours. Ammunition for this weapon has also been unlocked for all to use. It still costs in-game money to unlock, but no weapon score is required.
[*] We also replaced some existing loading screens with some gorgeous key art!
[/list]

[h3]IMPROVEMENTS[/h3]

[i][b]—  Performance[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Full rework of the animal home ranges, populations and schedules on Mississippi Acres Preserve, Vurhonga Savanna, Rancho Del Arroyo & Cuatro Colinas. This will boost the performance for users;
[/list]

[i][b]—  Graphics & Visual Effects[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Implemented FSR (FidelityFX Super Resolution) on PC platforms. This can be adjusted in [i]Settings> Graphics> AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0[/i], improving frame rate performance. For more information about FSR, visit the [url=https://www.amd.com/en/technologies/radeon-software-fidelityfx-super-resolution]AMD Website[/url].
[*] Improved sample pattern for SSAO (Screen Space Ambient Occlusion), improving shadows in the game;
[*] Improved the floating death animation for the Alligator;
[*] Third person animation setup has been revamped and most of the animations are improved;
[/list]

[i][b]—  Accessibility[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] New headline ‘Dog’ for dog related tutorial entries in Codex menu;
[*] Scent eliminator HUD improvements including duration indicator;
[*] Added Reticle to gameplay with different color variations. This helps aiming at objects for interactions, interacting with distant animal calls & spotting animals from a distance, and can help some players who experience motion sickness;
[*] Added an option in Settings to adjust Subtitles font size;
[*] Added option to remap Trophy Lodge inputs in Settings menu;
[/list]

[i][b]—  Miscellaneous[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Increased sensitivity of gamepad & mouse for all 1x magnification devices including Red dot, illuminated iron sight, reflex sight & all 1x scopes for relevant weapons;
[*] 10 point-to-point transport sites have been implemented along the riverbank in Mississippi Acres Preserve. At present, they won’t be visible on the map but that is something we will be addressing a little later this year. Just look for the boats!
[/list]

[h3][b]CONSIDERATIONS[/b][/h3]

[list]
[*] Full population resets will occur across Cuatro Colinas, Rancho del Arroyo, Mississippi Acres Preserve, and Vurhonga Savanna as a result of our optimization efforts. More information on this was mentioned above under Performance Improvements.
[*] The male black bears have decided to spice things up a little and are now going by the following descriptors: Black > Dusty; Dark > Black; Dusty > Dark.
[*] Updated the Medal icons designs on various screens;
[*] Added swimming icon for animal clues that are underwater;
[*] Geese cash rewards have been balanced to offset other fixes and harvest quantity.
[/list]

[h3][b]BUG FIXES[/b][/h3]

[b][i]—  Critical & Featured[/i][/b]

[list]
[*] Geese and Ducks will get attracted to callers;
[*] Fixed LOD issues for the female Red Deer which caused some to appear invisible at varying distances until the character is within about 50m;
[*] The Kullman .22H now provides a more appropriate bang for buck. The prices for the weapon and the ammo have also been slashed!
[/list]

[i][b]—   Animals & Environment[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Common Raccoon is now Class 2 animal instead of Class 1;
[*] Fixed an issue where disturbed vegetation was present near need zones only;
[*] Fixed the instance where sometimes corpses seemed to float in air after being shot from a long distance;
[*] The gates at Bingham Farms Mobile Home no longer levitate and fly around;
[/list]

[i][b]—   Weapons, Gear, & Character[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Fixed the issue of First Aid Kit not healing when used;
[*] Fixed an audio issue when switching between callers like Antler Rattler, Short Reed Canada Goose Caller;
[*] Fixed the problem where item could not be switched until sound ended while using Deer Bleat Caller & Roe Deer Caller;
[*] Fixed the issue of having infinite ammo if user kept firing while still in hip pose after running out of bullets;
[*] Manual and auto chambering mechanics for the Mangiafico, .410 while loaded with the .410 birdshot, has been corrected;
[*] The .270 Warden is now available for console players;
[*] Arrows retrieved from the field return to the players storage instead of their inventory;
[/list]

[i][b]—  User Interface & Multiplayer[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Fixed the issue with waypoints placement on Map on Ultrawide monitors;
[*] Fixed the incorrect icon for Dog biscuits on Inventory UI;
[*] Updated & fixed Decoy icon not being displayed in the HUD;
[*] Retrieved arrows will be available in the inventory now;
[*] Cash amount will not show cut off in UI if the value has more than 6 digits;
[*] Fixed the issue where multiple Turkey decoy POI markers were not being grouped together when placed very close to each other;
[*] Fixed the issue where Trophy lodge did not load for users other than the host in a MP session;
[*] Fixed the problem of users not being able to hear each other’s callers audio for Red deer, Moose, Elk caller(s) during MP;
[*] Fixed the issue of lures audio not working in MP;
[*] Fixed the issue where Great ones appeared as Diamonds to users other than the host in Multiplayer session;
[*] Geese caller will work for every player and not just the host in MP session;
[*] Scrollbar will function properly for description of items in Mission items menu in Codex for Rancho del Arroyo reserve;
[/list]

[i][b]—  Miscellaneous[/b][/i]

[list]
[*] Multiple crash fixes!
[/list]


[hr][/hr][b][h2]Need to report a bug or issue?[/h2][/b]
[url=https://support.thehunter.com/ style=button]Contact our Customer Support Team[/url]

Howdy Hunters!

Mississippi Acres Preserve is now available!

[h3]New Features[/h3]
[list]
[*] TruRACS is now enabled for the Lesser Kudu!
[*] Inspect feature for mission items: The mission items that users pick up are now placed in the Mission Item Codex and can be inspected. These items can hold valuable information!
[/list]
[h3]Improvements[/h3]
[list]
[*] Made FPS improvements to boost performance;
- Massive overhauls to animal update threading
- Improvements to population distribution on reserves (WIP)
- Increase LOD granularity across species needing LOD improvements
[*] Made fur quality (shader) improvements for all animals;
[*] Improved Feral Pig's model and textures;
[*] Improved Black Bear’s model and textures;
[*] Retouched visuals for water in lakes & rivers;
[*] Did a visual overhaul for some of the input icons and buttons;
[*] Updated feeding clue meshes for predators (nor more blood splatters);
[/list]

[h3]BUG FIXES[/h3]

[b]Critical & Featured[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed the issue of various Weapon Packs and Parque Fernando DLC missing from Xbox players’ libraries;
[*] Fixed the broken Fast travel issues across a number of reserves;
[*] Dog collision with player’s character is fixed;
[/list]

[b]---  Animals & Environment[/b]
[list]
[*] Radio towers across various reserves no longer defy gravity;
[*] Animals will not become un-harvestable if there are too many corpses unclaimed;
[*] Fixed the problem of EU rabbits not fleeing into their burrows as they should in Hirschfelden reserve;
[*] Sounds will not persist anymore after walking through bushes;
[*] Standardized fur rarity tier weighting for all species;
[*] Did a naming pass on all fur variations, all should have string names now (not ‘common’);
[/list]

[b]---  Weapons, Gear, & Character[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed the issue where Turkey callers were not included in Rancho Del Arroyo reserve;
[/list]

[b]---  User Interface & Multiplayer[/b]
[list]
[*] Multiplayer - Fixed a crash which could occur when showing waypoints to another player;
[*] Fixed an issue where discovering a new need zone caused the previously discovered need zone disappear on Map UI;
[*] Fixed the issue of not being able to input certain symbols and special characters into the Password field when creating an Avalanche Apex Connect™ account within game;
[/list]

Howdy Hunters,

It is our pleasure to introduce Rancho del Arroyo, inspired by the harsh, yet beautiful Sonoran desert of Northern Mexico, this stunning reserve includes five unique new animal species to hunt, new weaponry,  harsh biomes to explore, and a thrilling storyline that involves uncovering a century-old family mystery.

Please see the detailed patch notes (PC 1.68) for this update below. 

[h2]NEW FEATURES
[/h2]
▸   Added support for new paid DLC: Rancho del Arroyo

[h2]SPOTLIGHT BUG FIXES
[/h2]
  ▸   Diamond Whitetail Deer will no longer weigh more than 100kg;
   ▸   Backpacks will not be visible in first person camera;
   ▸   Fixed the slow motion bug for Dog at tracker level 1 and 16;
   ▸   Fixed the crash when user orders the dog to track within 50m of a rabbit corpse;
   ▸   Fixed the issue of tents disappearing with an active dog nearby when user resumes gameplay after quitting to main menu;
   ▸   Animal corpses will no longer be invisible after walking outside of render range and back;
   ▸   Fixed the issue of missing antlers on the trophies in the Trophy Lodge (this fix is not retroactive);
   ▸   Fixed the issue of ATV lights turning on/off at night time when 3rd person camera is toggled;

[h2]ADDITIONAL UPDATES
[/h2]

[h3]ANIMALS & ENVIRONMENT
[/h3]
   ▸   Reworked the spawning rates for Geese;
   ▸   Fixed the disappearing of Great One Whitetails that previously existed in the reserve's animal population after restarting the game;
   ▸   Dog will no more be slow in notifying user of a harvested animal;
   ▸   Buffalos near lookout tower will no longer cause damage to the user on 1st floor;
   ▸   Fixed the issue where Female Dog showed up even when user purchased Male Dog;

[h3]WEAPONS, GEAR, & CHARACTER
[/h3]
   ▸   Huntermate screen will not go invisible after switching reserves now;
   ▸   Fixed the issue where scope became invisible for a weapon while switching ammo types;
   ▸   [XB1] Fixed the issue of user’s character sliding/drifting during gameplay when controller is reconnected after being disconnected;
   ▸   Fixed the issue of sight disappearing on bows after switching to a different arrow type;
   ▸   Fixed the issue with Rangefinder bow sight not displaying range or aim dots;
   ▸   Fixed the issue when player could not jump or go prone after changing reserve while in a treestand;

[h3]USER INTERFACE & MULTIPLAYER
[/h3]
   ▸   Removed the black circle which appeared around waypoint marker;
   ▸   Removed & updated the placeholder text in My Dogs tab when user does not own any dog;
   ▸   Fixed the dog status icon while tracking live prey;
   ▸   The effective range stats for rifle ammo will no longer display low values in store and inventory;
   ▸   Fixed the issue where incorrect values were displayed for individual Reserve and Global    
   ▸   Play stats in Codex menu;
   ▸   Fixed the issue of user not being able to fast scroll through EULA popup using a controller;

[h3]MISCELLANEOUS
[/h3]
   ▸   User will be able to pet their dog in the Trophy Lodge;
   ▸   Dog will now gain a portion of total XP when starting to track a harvest and the rest of XP will be added when harvest is found;
   ▸   It will be easier now to complete the mission ‘The Perfect Liebre’ in Cuatro Colinas reserve;

[h3]IMPROVEMENTS[/h3]

   ▸   Our character artists worked their magic in updating color and fur textures for existing animals like Whitetail Deer, Mule Deer, Coyote, Bighorn Sheep & Merriam Turkey;
   ▸   User can now see other users’ waypoints in map during multiplayer session; 
   ▸   Made some Audio engine performance improvements;
   ▸   Refactored and standardized pricing for Multi Trophy Mounts;
   ▸   User’s character will get hurt by the cacti if they collide with them;
   ▸   Enabled footprints for dog in snow;
   ▸   Added a new (Carcass found) icon to notify user when dog is done with its harvest search;
   ▸   The maximum tracker level that Dog can achieve is 15 which is now indicated in Tracker Level icon on Dog screen;
   ▸   Dog will now sniff each blood spot more evidently while tracking blood clues;
   ▸   Added a checkmark to indicate which Dog is active in Kennel screen (if user has more than 1 dog);
   ▸   Now users can auto-run using a controller:
         ▸   Double click of L3 when standing still = Auto-walk
         ▸   Double click of L3 when walking or running = Auto-run
         ▸   One click of L3 = Toggle between auto-run and auto-walk

[h2]Greetings Hunters![/h2]

We’re here to give you an update on the state of the game, and also share a little insight into what the team is working on. 

[h3]To Recap...[/h3][hr][/hr]
In late March, we released the long-anticipated Bloodhound DLC for [i]theHunter: Call of the Wild[/i]. We cherished the awesome hunting stories that you shared with us and are so fortunate to have such a passionate community dedicated to our game.

Despite our efforts and positive testing results, the Bloodhound release wasn’t as smooth as we had hoped. For example, the ‘Tracker’ trait progression wasn’t working as intended, [i]and[/i] the Codex Scoring… Yeah, that too. 

We promptly addressed the situation in a ‘Message From the Developers’ update, and a few weeks after, a hotfix was deployed simultaneously across all platforms.  

[h3]What's Happening Next[/h3][hr][/hr]
While this update solved most of the hot-topic issues (but not all), it also, much to the detriment of the team, introduced new problems. As we’re sure most of you know, there are almost always risks involved when preparing and deploying a hotfix. Despite our best efforts to successfully resolve the issues we plan to address, sometimes stuff happens or there’s something we can’t see when testing on such a limited scale and we aren’t able to get it right. We really are sorry about this, and share your disappointment. 

While there is still much work to do, the team has been making good progress every day.
We’re not ready to commit to a date just yet, but we’ve prepared a solid list of issues that the team is actively working on. 

[b]Please keep in mind that we can’t guarantee that all these issues will be solved. We will however do our best to solve as many of them as possible. [/b]

Thank you again for all of your support and understanding! We’ll provide another update as soon as we can. 🧡

/ [i]The Call of the Wild Team[/i]

